    "body": "You mean, define their own version of \"create an event\"? I haven't checked, but it seems probable that e.g. HTML uses \"create an event\" to create mouse events... we'd have to go update HTML and any other specs to use the new UI events \"create an event\" instead of the DOM \"create an event\", if that's what you're suggesting.",
