    "created_at": "2018-03-13T08:20:45Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-03-13T08:20:45Z",
    "body": "So given what we need for \"relatedTargets\" (see #585) I'm thinking the event constructor calls an internal algorithm that by default is a no-op. (We might want to define it works for inheritance somehow too.)\r\n\r\nThat way we construct the object, then for the dictionary members we set those dictionary members that have a corresponding internal slot on the object. Then we call that internal algorithm which can handle the remainder, e.g., setting relatedTargets based on the provided relatedTarget, or the much more complicated equivalent operation for Touch Events.\r\n\r\nIt seems this should work for keyboard events too. We'd recommend against relying on this algorithm without filing an issue against this repository for advice, or some such.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
